{
  "schema": "lean-proof-simplification-evidence-v1",
  "source_commit": "b616cba766a6511da927585698861ae73e312d28",
  "scope": "Reuse matrix-free local-cell construction proofs",
  "independent_review": "passed; see independent/review.txt",
  "limitations": "The preliminary mixed-overlay prototype initially failed to locate PellHalf90; adding a cached fallback allowed it to compile, but the final paired checks use a separately recorded rebuild. Twenty-four changed or dependency-switched local prerequisites and five direct-client prerequisites were rebuilt; both target modules, CurrentWordConstruction and focused checks were then built in both phases. Source/object pins cover the 133-node expanded graph: 33 nodes rebuilt, 73 match supplied prior pins, and 27 historical Diophantine objects do not match a supplied prior receipt. Prior pins certify selected source/object pairs, not every transitive dependency. External packages and unmatched historical objects remain precompiled. Old namespace census has 86 declarations versus 40 final: 45 compiler-generated proof/simp auxiliaries and one unused private helper disappear. No tracked Lean/Python/Markdown/shell qualified-name references were found, and no removed generated name is a baseline default simp rule. Five defining equation listings and all 40 survivor type/axiom reports match byte-for-byte. Foundation Matrix co-import fails in both import orders in both phases with the same pre-existing naming collisions. Two warnings in the shared CurrentMasks prerequisite lack a paired preparation baseline; paired targets and clients and interface probes have no warnings. The matrix-free source change is documentation only. Full independent source-graph, command/record and generated-name review is archived. The archive omits compiled objects and external toolchain binaries.",
  "archive": "inputs-and-logs.zip",
